n":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.6.2.stable (mono, official build). The unconditional log is also still present in current master (`drivers/apple_embedded/apple_embedded.mm`).\n\n### System information\n\niOS 26.5.2 - Godot v4.6.2.stable.mono - iPhone 15 Pro (iPhone16,1)\n\n### Issue description\n\nEvery call to `Input.vibrate_handheld()` on iOS prints this to the Xcode console, even when the vibration works fine:\n\n```\nCould not vibrate using haptic engine: (null)\n```\n\nLooking at `AppleEmbedded::vibrate_haptic_engine` in `drivers/apple_embedded/apple_embedded.mm` (~line 114), the `NSLog` after starting the haptic pattern player runs unconditionally — there's no `if (error)` guard like the other haptic engine methods in the same file have (`get_haptic_engine_instance`, `start_haptic_engine`, `stop_haptic_engine`). Since `error` is nil on success, every successful vibrate logs the `(null)` line. `error` is also declared without being initialized to nil.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nExport any project to iOS, run it on a device from Xcode with the console open, and call `Input.vibrate_handheld()`. The log line appears on every call.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A — reproducible in a brand-new project with a single `Input.vibrate_handheld()` call.\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred